/* B.E. F.A.S.T. */
"Stroke symptoms come on suddenly. If you notice any one of these signs, call 911 or your local emergency number immediately. Fast treatment can save brain function." = "Gejala stroke muncul tiba-tiba. Jika Anda melihat salah satu tanda ini, segera hubungi 911 atau nomor darurat setempat (di Indonesia 119 atau 112). Penanganan cepat bisa menyelamatkan fungsi otak.";
"Sudden loss of balance or coordination, dizziness, or trouble walking." = "Tiba-tiba hilang keseimbangan atau koordinasi, pusing, atau sulit berjalan.";
"Sudden blurred or double vision, or loss of vision in one or both eyes." = "Tiba-tiba penglihatan kabur atau ganda, atau kehilangan penglihatan pada satu atau kedua mata.";
"One side of the face droops or feels numb. The smile may look uneven." = "Satu sisi wajah turun atau terasa kebas. Senyum bisa terlihat miring.";
"Sudden weakness or numbness in an arm or leg, often on one side of the body." = "Tiba-tiba lemah atau mati rasa pada lengan atau tungkai, sering di satu sisi tubuh.";
"Slurred speech, trouble speaking or understanding, or sudden confusion." = "Bicara pelo, sulit berbicara atau memahami, atau tiba-tiba bingung.";
"Call 911 right away, even if the symptoms go away. Note the time they started." = "Segera hubungi 911 atau nomor darurat setempat (di Indonesia 119 atau 112), meskipun gejalanya hilang. Catat waktu gejala dimulai.";

/* Types of stroke */
"Types of stroke" = "Jenis stroke";
"Strokes are caused either by a blockage or by bleeding. A TIA is a temporary warning." = "Stroke disebabkan oleh sumbatan atau perdarahan. TIA adalah peringatan sementara.";
"Ischemic stroke" = "Stroke iskemik";
"The most common type, about 87% of strokes." = "Jenis paling umum, sekitar 87% kasus stroke.";
"An ischemic stroke happens when a blood clot or narrowed artery blocks blood flow to part of the brain." = "Stroke iskemik terjadi ketika gumpalan darah atau arteri yang menyempit menghambat aliran darah ke sebagian otak.";
"Clot-dissolving medicine works best when given within a few hours of the first symptoms." = "Obat pelarut gumpalan darah paling efektif bila diberikan dalam beberapa jam setelah gejala pertama.";
"Doctors may also remove large clots with a catheter (thrombectomy)." = "Dokter juga bisa mengambil gumpalan besar dengan kateter (trombektomi).";
"Every minute counts, so call 911 or your local emergency number right away." = "Setiap menit berharga, jadi segera hubungi 911 atau nomor darurat setempat (di Indonesia 119 atau 112).";
"Hemorrhagic stroke" = "Stroke hemoragik";
"Less common, about 13% of strokes, but often more severe." = "Lebih jarang, sekitar 13% kasus stroke, tetapi sering lebih parah.";
"A hemorrhagic stroke happens when a weakened blood vessel breaks and bleeds into or around the brain, raising pressure and damaging tissue." = "Stroke hemoragik terjadi ketika pembuluh darah yang lemah pecah dan berdarah di dalam atau sekitar otak, sehingga tekanan naik dan jaringan rusak.";
"High blood pressure is a common cause." = "Tekanan darah tinggi adalah penyebab umum.";
"Treatment may include lowering blood pressure and surgery to stop the bleeding or relieve pressure." = "Pengobatan bisa berupa menurunkan tekanan darah dan operasi untuk menghentikan perdarahan atau mengurangi tekanan.";
"Aneurysms can be clipped or coiled to seal the vessel." = "Aneurisma bisa dijepit (clipping) atau diisi koil (coiling) untuk menutup pembuluh.";
"Transient ischemic attack" = "Serangan iskemik sementara";
"A \"mini-stroke\" with symptoms that go away." = "“Stroke ringan” yang gejalanya hilang sendiri.";
"A TIA is a brief blockage of blood flow to the brain. Its symptoms are the same as a stroke but usually last only minutes." = "TIA adalah sumbatan singkat aliran darah ke otak. Gejalanya sama dengan stroke, tetapi biasanya hanya berlangsung beberapa menit.";
"A TIA is a warning sign that a stroke may follow." = "TIA adalah tanda peringatan bahwa stroke bisa menyusul.";
"It needs emergency care, even if the symptoms are gone." = "Perlu penanganan darurat, meskipun gejalanya sudah hilang.";
"Treating the cause can prevent a future stroke." = "Mengobati penyebabnya dapat mencegah stroke di kemudian hari.";

/* Risk factors */
"Risk factors" = "Faktor risiko";
"Some conditions and habits make a stroke more likely. Many of them can be treated or changed." = "Beberapa penyakit dan kebiasaan membuat stroke lebih mungkin terjadi. Banyak di antaranya bisa diobati atau diubah.";
"High blood pressure" = "Tekanan darah tinggi";
"The leading cause of stroke. Over time it damages and weakens blood vessels." = "Penyebab utama stroke. Lama-kelamaan merusak dan melemahkan pembuluh darah.";
"Diabetes" = "Diabetes";
"High blood sugar damages blood vessels and makes clots more likely." = "Gula darah tinggi merusak pembuluh darah dan memudahkan terbentuknya gumpalan.";
"Heart disease" = "Penyakit jantung";
"Conditions such as atrial fibrillation (AFib) can cause clots that travel to the brain." = "Kondisi seperti fibrilasi atrium dapat menimbulkan gumpalan darah yang terbawa ke otak.";
"Smoking" = "Merokok";
"Damages blood vessels and raises blood pressure." = "Merusak pembuluh darah dan menaikkan tekanan darah.";
"Sleep apnea" = "Apnea tidur";
"Repeated pauses in breathing during sleep strain the heart and blood vessels." = "Napas yang berulang kali berhenti saat tidur membebani jantung dan pembuluh darah.";
"Drug use" = "Penggunaan narkoba";
"Drugs such as cocaine and amphetamines can trigger a stroke, even in young people." = "Narkoba seperti kokain dan amfetamin bisa memicu stroke, bahkan pada orang muda.";

/* Prevention */
"Lower your risk" = "Turunkan risiko Anda";
"Most strokes are linked to risk factors you can manage. These habits help at any age." = "Sebagian besar stroke berkaitan dengan faktor risiko yang bisa Anda kendalikan. Kebiasaan ini membantu di usia berapa pun.";
"Control blood pressure" = "Kendalikan tekanan darah";
"Check it regularly and take medicine as prescribed." = "Periksa secara rutin dan minum obat sesuai resep.";
"Manage blood sugar" = "Kendalikan gula darah";
"Keep diabetes under control with your care team." = "Kendalikan diabetes bersama tim medis Anda.";
"Manage cholesterol" = "Kendalikan kolesterol";
"Ask your doctor how often to get it checked." = "Tanyakan ke dokter seberapa sering perlu diperiksa.";
"Quit smoking and tobacco" = "Berhenti merokok";
"Your risk starts dropping soon after you quit." = "Risiko mulai turun tak lama setelah berhenti.";
"Stay active" = "Tetap aktif";
"Aim for about 30 minutes of moderate activity most days." = "Usahakan sekitar 30 menit aktivitas sedang hampir setiap hari.";
"Eat a heart-healthy diet" = "Makan sehat untuk jantung";
"More vegetables, fruit and whole grains; less salt and processed food." = "Lebih banyak sayur, buah, dan biji-bijian utuh; lebih sedikit garam dan makanan olahan.";
"Keep a healthy weight" = "Jaga berat badan sehat";
"Even modest weight loss can lower blood pressure." = "Turun berat badan sedikit saja bisa menurunkan tekanan darah.";
"Sleep well" = "Tidur cukup";
"Aim for 7 to 9 hours, and get checked if you snore heavily." = "Tidur 7 sampai 9 jam, dan periksakan diri jika Anda mendengkur keras.";

/* Treatments */
"Treatment depends on the type of stroke and how quickly it begins. The sooner, the better." = "Pengobatan tergantung jenis stroke dan seberapa cepat dimulai. Makin cepat, makin baik.";
"Clot-dissolving medicine" = "Obat pelarut gumpalan darah";
"Medicine given through an IV to break up a clot." = "Obat yang diberikan lewat infus untuk menghancurkan gumpalan darah.";
"For ischemic stroke, a clot-dissolving medicine such as tPA can restore blood flow to the brain." = "Pada stroke iskemik, obat pelarut gumpalan seperti tPA dapat memulihkan aliran darah ke otak.";
"Works best when started within 3 to 4.5 hours of the first symptoms." = "Paling efektif bila dimulai dalam 3 sampai 4,5 jam setelah gejala pertama.";
"Can improve recovery and reduce disability." = "Dapat membantu pemulihan dan mengurangi kecacatan.";
"Not used when there is a high risk of bleeding, such as after recent surgery." = "Tidak digunakan jika risiko perdarahan tinggi, misalnya setelah operasi baru-baru ini.";
"Mechanical thrombectomy" = "Trombektomi mekanis";
"A catheter procedure to remove a large clot." = "Tindakan dengan kateter untuk mengambil gumpalan besar.";
"A thin tube is guided through an artery to the brain, where doctors remove the clot directly." = "Selang tipis dimasukkan lewat arteri hingga ke otak, lalu dokter mengambil gumpalan secara langsung.";
"Can be done up to 24 hours after symptoms start for some patients." = "Pada sebagian pasien bisa dilakukan hingga 24 jam setelah gejala mulai.";
"Often used together with clot-dissolving medicine for strokes in large arteries." = "Sering dikombinasikan dengan obat pelarut gumpalan untuk stroke di arteri besar.";
"Restores blood flow quickly to limit brain damage." = "Memulihkan aliran darah dengan cepat untuk membatasi kerusakan otak.";
"Surgery for bleeding" = "Operasi perdarahan";
"Procedures to stop bleeding and relieve pressure." = "Tindakan untuk menghentikan perdarahan dan mengurangi tekanan.";
"In a hemorrhagic stroke, surgery may be needed to stop the bleeding and lower pressure on the brain." = "Pada stroke hemoragik, mungkin diperlukan operasi untuk menghentikan perdarahan dan mengurangi tekanan pada otak.";
"An aneurysm can be clipped or coiled to seal the bleeding vessel." = "Aneurisma bisa dijepit atau diisi koil untuk menutup pembuluh yang berdarah.";
"A craniotomy can remove pooled blood and relieve pressure." = "Kraniotomi dapat membuang darah yang menumpuk dan mengurangi tekanan.";
"Quick treatment helps prevent further brain injury." = "Penanganan cepat membantu mencegah kerusakan otak lebih lanjut.";
"Rehabilitation" = "Rehabilitasi";
"Therapy to regain skills after a stroke." = "Terapi untuk memulihkan kemampuan setelah stroke.";
"Recovery often continues for months. Rehabilitation helps people relearn movement, speech and everyday tasks." = "Pemulihan sering berlangsung berbulan-bulan. Rehabilitasi membantu belajar kembali bergerak, berbicara, dan melakukan kegiatan sehari-hari.";
"May include physical, occupational and speech therapy." = "Bisa mencakup fisioterapi, terapi okupasi, dan terapi wicara.";
"Starting early, while still in the hospital, tends to help." = "Memulai lebih awal, saat masih di rumah sakit, biasanya membantu.";
"Family and caregivers are an important part of recovery." = "Keluarga dan pendamping adalah bagian penting dari pemulihan.";

